These vectors are vendored verbatim from

    https://github.com/sirosfoundation/siros-dc-matcher
    crates/siros-dc-matcher-core/tests/vectors/circuit_zk_response

commit fe9020f (the head of
https://github.com/sirosfoundation/siros-dc-matcher/pull/49, which adds the
x5chain member). RE-PIN TO THE MERGE COMMIT once that pull request lands: a
branch head can be rewritten, and a pin to one is a pin to nothing.

The normative text is docs/circuit_zk_response.md in that repository.

They are the shared conformance set for every implementation that validates a
circuit_zk presentation - the Rust matcher, the Kotlin and Swift SDKs, and this
verifier. Vendored rather than fetched so the test suite does not depend on the
network.

The vendored copy is pinned twice in circuit_zk_response_vectors_test.go: once
under a digest over names and contents, and once under the manifest digest the
matcher repository publishes,

    ls *.json | LC_ALL=C sort | xargs sha256sum | sha256sum
    421ecfe003fd41559375fe225fbd80432afc65fc83d1232344599dbb3401ee8a

so the number quoted upstream can be compared against this copy directly.

Re-vendor rather than edit: a local change turns a cross-implementation check
into a self-consistency one that passes while the implementations disagree.
